> **ADMIRAL BYRD: BEYOND THE ICE** <

> _INTRODUCTION SCENE_ <

FADE IN:

EXT. ANTARCTICA - SUNSET

Words type out across the screen, letter by letter, as if on an old typewriter, in typewriter font. Each key CLACKS:

SUPER: "ADMIRAL BYRD 1934: ANTARCTICA"

BYRD, alone in the vast, isolated Antarctic winter. Not a soul in sight. The WIND HOWLING.

Sunset incoming.

Byrd, ill, violently COUGHING his guts up.

He cooks a large piece of meat on the fire, on a skewer resting across two metal bars.

The meat SIZZLES.

He takes the meat off and begins to eat it, facing the desolate area of nothingness.

Pause.

Byrd, just eating the meat.

Just as he is about to go to his tent, five meters away, he sees a FLICKER on the horizon.

Byrd looks startled, a tad uncertain, as he tries to make out what's happening in the distance.

In his eyes, you see his motivation to conquer the unknown in the distance.

The camera turns off Byrd, panning 90 degrees from side-on, to just the endless ice desert.

The remoteness sinks in.

CUT TO BLACK.

> END OF INTRODUCTION SCENE <

MAIN TITLE CARD, over black. The MUSIC swells:

> **ADMIRAL BYRD: BEYOND THE ICE** <
